WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:10.992
After the big event wraps up and you finally get home exhausted, the most important last step is a safe, thorough cleanse.

2
00:00:11.328 --> 00:00:16.320
Don't force a brush through hair set with lots of bobby pins and strong-hold spray —

3
00:00:16.656 --> 00:00:24.816
carefully and slowly remove the hair ornament and decorative pins first, then take out the hidden bobby pins one by one.

4
00:00:25.152 --> 00:00:32.568
Before shampooing, wet your hair thoroughly with lukewarm water, rinse with conditioner first, then follow with shampoo.

5
00:00:32.904 --> 00:00:40.680
This softens the stiff spray residue so the shampoo step afterward cleans thoroughly without tangling.

6
00:00:41.016 --> 00:00:45.432
The makeup is also a long-wear, high-adherence formula,

7
00:00:45.768 --> 00:00:52.968
so be sure to use a cleansing oil, massaging it warm against your skin to fully dissolve the makeup, then follow with a foam cleanser for a second wash.

8
00:00:53.304 --> 00:00:59.784
Rinse thoroughly, then give your skin plenty of moisture to recover from hours under the weight of the hanbok and makeup,

9
00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:04.752
and it's a good idea to let your skin rest for a day with just a generous layer of moisturizer.

10
00:01:05.088 --> 00:01:10.392
That way, you can return to your normal routine the next day without breakouts or puffiness.
